t/advanced-usage.html#tls-warnings\n  warnings.warn(\n/root/.local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/urllib3/connectionpool.py:1097: InsecureRequestWarning: Unverified HTTPS request is being made to host '127.0.0.1'. Adding certificate verification is strongly advised. See: https://urllib3.readthedocs.io/en/latest/advanced-usage.html#tls-warnings\n  warnings.warn(\n/root/.local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/urllib3/connectionpool.py:1097: InsecureRequestWarning: Unverified HTTPS request is being made to host '127.0.0.1'. Adding certificate verification is strongly advised. See: https://urllib3.readthedocs.io/en/latest/advanced-usage.html#tls-warnings\n  warnings.warn(\n/root/.local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/urllib3/connectionpool.py:1097: InsecureRequestWarning: Unverified HTTPS request is being made to host '127.0.0.1'. Adding certificate verification is strongly advised. See: https://urllib3.readthedocs.io/en/latest/advanced-usage.html#tls-warnings\n  warnings.warn(\n总成交: 98 笔\n\n📊 累计战绩 (4月至今)\n完整回合: 53\n胜: 2 | 负: 3 | 平: 48\n胜率: 40.0%\n累计已实现盈亏: -2.86 USDT\n\n📅 月度明细:\n  2026-04: 2/5 = 40.0% | PnL -2.86U\n","name":"cd /root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784825247825}}
{"type":"message","id":"6b7d9cb7","parentId":"9970f2d9","timestamp":"2026-07-23T16:47:48.369Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, got the data. But wait - 98 trades, 53 round trips, but only 5 have non-zero PnL (2 wins, 3 losses), and 48 breakevens. That's suspicious - most trades have 0 realized PnL. This is because my FIFO matching might not be correct.\n\nThe issue is: when a BUY is partially matched by a SELL, the remaining BUY quantity stays in the queue. And the PnL from that SELL is attributed to all the BUYs it matched. But when the SELL matches multiple BUY entries, I'm counting the same PnL multiple times.\n\nActually wait, let me re-examine. With FIFO:\n- BUY 0.003 BTC → queue\n- SELL 0.003 BTC → matches the BUY, BUY is fully consumed → count round trip with PnL from this SELL\nBut the issue is the PnL is on the SELL trade. One SELL could match against multiple BUYs. The PnL from the SELL should be attributed to all matched BUYs proportionally.\n\nActually, looking at it more carefully, the problem is that PnL from the SELL closes the position that was opened by one or more BUYs. If one SELL matches against 2 BUYs, both BUYs are fully consumed (since the SELL qty = BUY1 qty + BUY2 qty). The PnL from this one SELL is attributed to both BUY round trips - which double-counts.\n\nActually, in the fixed version above, the `while` loop iterates but uses the same `pnl` for each matched BUY. That means if one SELL closes 2 BUY positions, both get the same PnL value, which is wrong.\n\nBut actually, with positionSide=BOTH, each SELL closes the entire position. The realizedPnl on the SELL is the total PnL for that closing. If the SELL qty = sum of multiple BUYs, the PnL should be split proportionally.\n\nHowever, looking at the data - 98 trades, 53 round trips, but only 5 with non-zero PnL. That means most trades have 0 realizedPnl. This could be because:\n1. The `realizedPnl` field is 0 for most trades (maybe only the final partial sell that closes everything has the PnL)\n2. Or my matching is wrong\n\nLet me look at the raw trades more carefully. Let me check what the realizedPnl values look like across all trades.\n\nActually, for a simpler approach, let me just count completed round trips differently. For each side change in the same symbol, consider it one round trip, and use the PnL from the closing trade.\n\nBut wait, 48 breakevens is suspicious. Let me look at actual PnL values.\n\nAh wait, actually looking at the BTC trade data from earlier:\n- BUY: realizedPnl = \"-3.59430000\"  (a BUY with negative PnL!)\n- SELL: realizedPnl = \"0\"\n\nThe BUY has non-zero PnL while SELL has 0 PnL. That's because with Binance futures, the PnL is realized on the trade that reduces the position, regardless of whether it's BUY or SELL.\n\nSo the PnL can appear on BUY or SELL trades depending on which reduces position size. My logic only counts PnL from SELL closes BUY, but what about SELL→BUY (short positions)?\n\nLet me rethink: with positionSide=BOTH:\n- BUY increases long / decreases short\n- SELL decreases long / increases short\n\nThe PnL is on whichever trade reduces the position. So I need to handle both directions:\n- BUY closes a SHORT → realizedPnl on BUY\n- SELL closes a LONG → realizedPnl on SELL\n\nAlso, the issue is that I'm only looking at SELL matching BUYs, but SELLs that open shorts wouldn't have matching BUYs. I need to handle both directions.\n\nThis is getting complex. Let me simplify: instead of FIFO matching, let me just pair consecutive opposite-side trades with non-zero PnL. Or better yet, let me count all trades with non-zero realizedPnl as completed round trips.\n\nActually, the simplest approach: count all trades where realizedPnl != 0. Those are the closing trades. Each represents a completed round trip.\n\nLet me just check how many trades have non-zero PnL.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_c1AqvDOv6nuMmcbSEigv1496","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 << 'PYEOF'\nimport json, time, sys\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nsys.path.insert(0, '.')\nimport binance_auto_trade as bat\n\nsymbols = ['BTC','ETH','SOL','BNB','DOT','LINK','XRP']\nstart = int(time.mktime(time.strptime('2026-04-01','%Y-%m-%d'))) * 1000\n\nall_trades = []\nfor sym in symbols:\n    r = bat.request('GET', '/fapi/v1/userTrades',\n                    {'symbol': f'{sym}USDT', 'startTime': start, 'limit': 1000})\n    if isinstance(r, list):\n        all_trades.extend(r)\n\nall_trades.sort(key=lambda x: x['time'])\n\n# Check PnL values\npnl_trades = [t for t in all_trades if abs(float(t.get('realizedPnl', 0) or 0)) > 0.001]\nprint(f'有非零PnL的交易: {len(pnl_trades)}')\nfor t in pnl_trades[:20]:\n    pnl = float(t['realizedPnl'])\n    print(f'  {t[\"symbol\"]} {t[\"side\"]} qty={t[\"qty\"]} PnL={pnl:+.4f} time={time.strftime(\"%m-%d %H:%M\", time.localtime(t[\"time\"]/1000))}')\n\n# Count by direction\ntotal_pnl = sum(float(t.get('realizedPnl', 0) or 0) for t in pnl_trades)\nwins = sum(1 for t in pnl_trades if float(t['realizedPnl']) > 0.001)\nlosses = sum(1 for t in pnl_trades if float(t['realizedPnl']) < -0.001)\nprint(f'\\n共 {len(pnl_trades)} 次平仓')\nprint(f'胜: {wins} | 负: {losses}')\nprint(f'胜率: {wins/(wins+losses)*100:.1f}%')\nprint(f'累计已实现: {total_pnl:+.2f} USDT')\nPYEOF","timeout":60}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":772,"output":2497,"cacheRead":41216,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":44485,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784825247910}}
